ss=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years back to 1951, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 37 of them on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids. In 2025, November to December finished at 55% of normal on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, February to March sits at 57% and March to April at 60% on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 2007, with grid 18479 at 62%.</p>"}
